sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 6, docs/reference/development-containers.md#threads-and-tasks): Conn's own flow when a user starts a thread in an Orbit Project. It uses only public Orbit operations and T3's own API; Conn is drawn because this is Conn's flow, not a command chart. A task that attaches later drives the same thread.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · Conn thread start
  %% kind: none
  autonumber
  %% lane CONN icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane T3 icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CONN as Conn<br/>user's device
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant T3 as T3 server<br/>in the container
  Note over CONN: Start a thread<br/>Orbit Project · message
  %%> What the user does:
  %%> - picks an Orbit Project and a Node, and writes the first message
  %%> What Conn proposes:
  %%> - an Instance name from the message, and the Project's default Instance as `--from` when it exists (open question 3 in the plan)
  CONN->>GW: instance:create<br/>PROJECT NODE NAME
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the device's Node has node access to the target Node, the same edge that Conn needs to pair
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-create
  GW-->>CONN: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  SW->>T3: Create the Instance<br/>container/create.mmd
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the whole create: copy, workspace, database, first T3 start, setup, Processes, Route, Gateway session
  SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
  Note over GW: Record Instance, T3 server
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CONN->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CONN: active · environment id
  end
  CONN->>GW: Pair with the server<br/>conn pairing create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the usual pairing: Swamp mints a one-time link with the Gateway's session on this T3 server
  GW-->>CONN: pairing_url
  CONN->>T3: Pair, then start thread<br/>first message · model
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Conn opens the pairing link, then starts the thread in the Instance's T3 project `/srv/workspace` with the first message
  %%> - from here Conn talks to the T3 server directly over WireGuard, as with any T3 server
  T3-->>CONN: Turn streams<br/>diffs · terminal · browser
  opt a task attaches to the Instance
    SW->>T3: Drive the thread<br/>T3 MCP · thread send
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - while the task flow runs, Swamp sends turns with `queue`, waits for each and reads the result, with the Gateway's session
    %%> - the user sees every turn in the same thread; a message the user sends during a turn is queued by T3
    %%> When the task pauses:
    %%> - Swamp sends nothing more, and the user drives from the thread
  end
